{"chunk_id": "ee2dfb2bbc2b", "text": "This passage recounts a pivotal episode in Karna\u2019s life. While his teacher Parashurama (Rama of the Bhrigu line) sleeps with his head on Karna\u2019s lap, a monstrous worm burrows into Karna\u2019s thigh. Karna endures unbearable pain in silence so as not to disturb his guru, demonstrating extraordinary endurance and devotion. The worm turns out to be a cursed Asura freed by Parashurama\u2019s presence. But the blood awakens the sage, who realizes that no Brahmana could endure such agony; suspecting deception, he forces Karna to reveal that he is not a Brahmana but of mixed or lower birth. Angered by the lie used to obtain divine weapons, Parashurama curses Karna so that the Brahma weapon will fail him when he most needs it. The section then shifts to a royal self-choice ceremony where Duryodhana abducts a princess, with Karna fiercely defending him against assembled kings.\nKarna endures a worm\u2019s torment while Parashurama sleeps, revealing his non\u2011Brahmin identity and earning a curse before later aiding Duryodhana in abducting a princess.\nThemes: Karna's endurance, guru deception and curse, fate and identity, release from curse, royal abduction and rivalry", "vector": [0.010460936464369297, -0.014210059307515621, -0.004525388590991497, -0.005786396097391844, 0.0051660616882145405, 0.020460858941078186, -0.022915076464414597, -0.016393093392252922, -0.029287908226251602, -0.03023705445230007, 0.015362593345344067, 0.013993112370371819, 0.013064305298030376, 0.010779577307403088, -0.009667721576988697, -0.005945716518908739, 0.04881318286061287, -0.0027881141286343336, 0.026562506332993507, -0.02524726279079914, 0.014142263680696487, -0.006088088732212782, -0.008121971040964127, 0.027552329003810883, -0.022454064339399338, 0.020230352878570557, 0.020826958119869232, -0.029179435223340988, 0.012630410492420197, -0.02698284201323986, -0.0004406745720189065, -0.003738954197615385, -0.016040554270148277, -0.0175456274